{%- comment -%}
  Renders the shirt bundle promotion callout.

  Accepts:
  - show_subtext: {Boolean} adds a supporting line under the headline. The cart
    page and drawer have room for it; the add-to-cart notification does not.

  Usage:
  {% render 'shirt-promotion', show_subtext: true %}

  The shirt count is computed here from cart.items rather than in JavaScript.
  The previous approach counted DOM rows: each cart row carried a data-is-shirt
  attribute and a ShirtPromotion class in cart.js / cart-drawer.js summed them,
  then toggled a #shirt-promotion-section element. Two bugs came out of that.
  Both the drawer and the cart page emitted those same ids, so on /cart with the
  drawer enabled getElementById only ever found the drawer's copy and the cart
  page's callout never appeared; and the row query was unscoped, so it summed
  drawer rows and cart-page rows together and double-counted every shirt.

  Counting server-side removes that whole class of bug: no ids, no global
  queries, and collection membership as the source of truth. Every surface that
  renders this sits inside a container the Section Rendering API replaces on
  cart change (.js-contents on the cart page, .drawer__inner in the drawer, the
  notification's own section), so the message stays in sync with the cart.

  Collection membership means newly added shirts are picked up with no code
  change, as long as they are in one of these collections.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign shirt_collections = 'shirts,long-sleeve-western-shirts,fishing-shirts' | split: ','
  assign shirt_count = 0

  for item in cart.items
    assign is_shirt = false

    assign item_type = item.product.type | downcase
    if item_type contains 'shirt'
      assign is_shirt = true
    else
      for collection in item.product.collections
        if shirt_collections contains collection.handle or collection.id == 478689722404
          assign is_shirt = true
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif

    if is_shirt
      assign shirt_count = shirt_count | plus: item.quantity
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if shirt_count > 0 -%}
  {%- if shirt_count == 1 -%}
    <a
      href="{{ collections.shirts.url | default: '/collections/shirts' }}"
      class="shirt-promotion shirt-promotion--offer"
    >
      <span class="shirt-promotion__icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <i class="fa-regular fa-message-dollar"></i>
      </span>
      <span class="shirt-promotion__text">
        <strong>Add one more shirt (any style) and save $15</strong>
        {%- if show_subtext -%}
          <span class="shirt-promotion__subtext">
            You have 1 shirt in your cart — add another to unlock $15 off.
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
      <span class="shirt-promotion__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
    </a>
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="shirt-promotion shirt-promotion--earned">
      <span class="shirt-promotion__icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <i class="fa-regular fa-face-cowboy-hat"></i>
      </span>
      <span class="shirt-promotion__text">
        <strong>You're saving $15 by ordering 2 or more</strong>
        {%- if show_subtext -%}
          <span class="shirt-promotion__subtext">
            Nice pick. 2 or more shirts means $15 off your order.
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
